\v 2 “I¦155937 know¦155937 about your¦155940 activities and¦155941 work¦155943, and¦155945 your¦155948 endurance¦155947 and¦155949 that¦155950 you¦155952 can't tolerate¦155953 evil¦155954 \add >people\add*, and¦155955 that you've¦155956 investigated the¦155958 ones who call themselves¦155961 missionaries¦155963 but¦155965 are not, and¦155968 you've¦155969 found¦155969 them¦155970 to be frauds.
\v 3 \add I'm aware that\add* you've¦155976 endured and¦155980 even suffered \add persecution\add* because¦155982 you've \add believed in\add* me¦155985, but¦155987 you've¦155990 never given up.
\v 4 However, I¦155993 do have¦155993 something against¦155994 you¦155995: you've abandoned the¦155997 love¦155998 that¦155996 you¦155999 first¦156001 had.
\v 5 So¦156007 \add now, you need to\add* remember¦156006 where¦156008 you've¦156009 fallen¦156009 from, and¦156011 repent¦156012 and¦156013 repeat how you behaved at the¦156014 beginning, but¦156019 if¦156018 you don't¦156020, I'll¦156021 come¦156021 to¦156022 you¦156022 and¦156025 if¦156034 you¦156036 don't repent¦156036, I'll remove¦156026 your¦156029 lampstand¦156028 from its¦156033 place¦156032.
\v 6 But¦156037 you do have this¦156038 going for you¦156040: you¦156042 hate¦156042 what the \add disciples of\add* Nicolaus are doing,\f + \fr 2:7 \ft Nicolaus' disciples ate food that had been sacrificed to idols and committed sexual sins.\f* just like I¦156048 do.
\p
\v 7 Everyone who wants to understand needs¦156053 to listen¦156053 to what¦156054 \add &God's¦156055\add* \nd spirit¦156056\nd* is¦156057 saying¦156057 to¦156058 the¦156058 assemblies¦156060.
