\v 12 To¦156201 the¦156201 assembly's¦156206 messenger¦156202 in¦156204 Pergamum write¦156207:
\p The one with the¦156216 sharp¦156217 sword¦156213 says¦156209 these¦156208 \add >things\add*:
\v 13 “I¦156218 know¦156218 where¦156223 you¦156224 live¦156224: where¦156225 Satan's¦156229 throne¦156227 is¦156229. Despite that, you firmly \add believe in me\add* and you haven't denied¦156238 your faith¦156240 in me¦156241, even¦156242 when Antipas¦156249, the¦156253 faithful¦156254 \add man who told others about me\add* was¦156257 killed¦156257 in your \add city\add*, where¦156260 Satan¦156263 lives¦156264.
\v 14 But¦156265 I¦156266 do have¦156266 a¦156269 few¦156269 \add >things\add* against¦156267 you¦156268: you¦156271 have¦156271 some¦156271 people there¦156273 who¦156278 hold¦156274 to \add the ancient prophet\add* Balaam's¦156277 teaching¦156280.\x + \xo 2:14: \xt Num 22:5,7; 31:16; Deu 23:4.\x* He taught \add Moab's king\add*, Balak¦156284, how to¦156287 \add ≈tempt¦156288\add* the¦156290 Israelis¦156292 and to¦156294 eat¦156294 \add food\add* that had been sacrificed¦156295 to idols¦156295, and¦156296 to¦156297 be sexually¦156297 immoral¦156297.\x + \xo 2:14: \xt Num 25:1-3.\x*
