\v 20 But¦156429 I¦156430 have¦156430 against¦156431 you¦156432 that¦156435 you¦156436 tolerate¦156436 that woman¦156439 Jezebel¦156442\x + \xo 2:20: \xt 1Ki 16:31; 2Ki 9:22,30.\x* who calls¦156446 herself¦156448 a¦156451 prophetess¦156451, and¦156453 she¦156454 deceives my¦156460 servants¦156461 by teaching¦156454 them to¦156462 be sexually¦156462 immoral¦156462 and¦156463 to¦156464 eat¦156464 \add food that's been\add* offered to idols¦156465.
\v 21 Even though I've¦156468 given¦156468 her¦156469 time¦156470 to repent, she's \add still\add* not¦156474 willing¦156476 to¦156477 turn away from her¦156482 immorality¦156480.
\v 22 Listen, I'm¦156488 going to¦156491 \add punish her with a terrible sickness\add*, and¦156494 to punish those who are committing¦156496 adultery¦156496 with¦156497 her¦156498 with terrible suffering if¦156502 they¦156505 don't¦156503 turn away from what she's doing.
\v 23 I¦156515 will¦156515 kill¦156515 her¦156514 children¦156513, then¦156518 all¦156520 the¦156521 assemblies¦156522 will know¦156519 that¦156523 I¦156524 am¦156525 the¦156526 one who searches¦156527 \add people's\add* affections and¦156529 hearts¦156530,\x + \xo 2:23: \xt Psa 7:9; Jer 17:10.\x* and¦156531 who \add punishes or rewards\add* each¦156534 one of¦156538 you¦156538 depending on your actions¦156537.\x + \xo 2:23: \xt Psa 62:12.\x*
