\v 2 So wake up \add from the dead\add* and¦156674 strengthen¦156675 what's left¦156680 and was¦156680 about to¦156683 die¦156683, because¦156685 your¦156687 actions¦156689 have¦156690 been¦156690 inadequate in \nd God's¦156693\nd* sight.
\v 3 Remember¦156695 how¦156697 you¦156698 \add first\add* listened¦156700 to and¦156699 internalised \add God's message\add*, and¦156701 how you obeyed it¦156702 and¦156703 repented¦156704. If¦156706 you¦156709 don't wake up \add soon\add*, I'll¦156711 come¦156711 \add unexpectedly\add*—you'll certainly not¦156718 know¦156719 \add in advance\add* when I'll¦156724 be¦156724 coming¦156724.\x + \xo 3:3: \xt Mat 24:43-44; Luk 12:39-40; Rev 16:15.\x*
\v 4 But¦156727 you¦156728 do have¦156728 a¦156729 few¦156729 people in¦156733 Sardis¦156734 who¦156735 haven't stained¦156737 their¦156741 records, and¦156742 because¦156750 they are worthy¦156751, they'll¦156743 \add be\add* dressed¦156739 in¦156748 white¦156749 and walk¦156743 with¦156746 me¦156747.
\v 5 \add So\add* anyone who conquers will¦156757 be¦156757 dressed¦156757 like that in¦156759 \add pure\add* white¦156761, and¦156762 I¦156765 certainly won't¦156764 erase¦156765 their names¦156767 from¦156769 the¦156770 Book¦156771 of¦156773 Life¦156773,\x + \xo 3:5: \xt Exo 32:32-33; Psa 69:28; Rev 20:12.\x* but¦156774 I'll¦156776 declare their names¦156778 to my¦156784 father¦156783 and¦156785 to his messengers¦156788.\x + \xo 3:5: \xt Mat 10:32; Luk 12:8.\x*
\p
